{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "chapter-02",
  "bookId": "sleepy-hollow",
  "number": 2,
  "title": "The Midnight Rider",
  "level": "a2",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p-01",
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Ichabod’s heart beat fast. He turned in the "
        },
        {
          "text": "saddle",
          "vocabId": "saddle"
        },
        {
          "text": " and looked behind him. A tall man in a black "
        },
        {
          "text": "cloak",
          "vocabId": "cloak"
        },
        {
          "text": " rode a big black horse. The "
        },
        {
          "text": "stranger",
          "vocabId": "stranger"
        },
        {
          "text": " did not speak. His hat was low, and under it there was nothing — no face, no eyes. Ichabod felt cold, although the night was warm. A few minutes before, he had been laughing at the party. Now he remembered the old story: the headless rider of Sleepy Hollow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-02",
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Go, Gunpowder, go!” he said. The old horse began to "
        },
        {
          "text": "gallop",
          "vocabId": "gallop"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but the black horse stayed close. Ichabod could hear its "
        },
        {
          "text": "hooves",
          "vocabId": "hooves"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the road, slow and heavy, like a drum. He held the "
        },
        {
          "text": "reins",
          "vocabId": "reins"
        },
        {
          "text": " tight and looked for the "
        },
        {
          "text": "bridge",
          "vocabId": "bridge"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The story said the rider could not cross the "
        },
        {
          "text": "stream",
          "vocabId": "stream"
        },
        {
          "text": ". If he reached the bridge, he would be safe. The black horse came closer, and Ichabod hit the old horse with his heels."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-03",
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The road went through the dark trees. "
        },
        {
          "text": "branches",
          "vocabId": "branches"
        },
        {
          "text": " moved in the wind, and the rider’s "
        },
        {
          "text": "shadow",
          "vocabId": "shadow"
        },
        {
          "text": " grew longer on the ground. The "
        },
        {
          "text": "hooves",
          "vocabId": "hooves"
        },
        {
          "text": " sounded like an "
        },
        {
          "text": "echo",
          "vocabId": "echo"
        },
        {
          "text": " behind him. Ichabod tried to "
        },
        {
          "text": "race",
          "vocabId": "race"
        },
        {
          "text": " the stranger, but his horse was old and "
        },
        {
          "text": "tired",
          "vocabId": "tired"
        },
        {
          "text": ". The bridge was near. He could see the white mist over the water and the black shape of the rider beside him. His hands were wet on the reins."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-04",
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "At the last "
        },
        {
          "text": "bend",
          "vocabId": "bend"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Ichabod looked back. The rider was closer than before. He was so "
        },
        {
          "text": "terrified",
          "vocabId": "terrified"
        },
        {
          "text": " that he did not see the low branch above the "
        },
        {
          "text": "path",
          "vocabId": "path"
        },
        {
          "text": ". It hit his head, and his hat fell into the stream. He did not stop. The bridge was only a few steps away. Behind him, the black horse made no sound at all. It was as silent as a ghost."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-05",
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "On the bridge, Ichabod turned his horse. The stranger stopped too. For a second, nobody moved. Then the rider stood up in his "
        },
        {
          "text": "saddle",
          "vocabId": "saddle"
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "throw",
          "vocabId": "throw"
        },
        {
          "text": " something dark and round. It flew through the air, and Ichabod raised his arms. He tried to run, but the thing hit him with a heavy sound. Everything went black. The last thing he heard was the stream under the bridge."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
